 # bench-mineru-api (benchmark fixture)
 
 A document-parsing tool plugin with a host RPC channel (`/mineru-api`) that its
-browser settings page reads/writes, written in the 0.1.1-era style. The host is
-moving to dsh 0.1.2-alpha.2.
+browser settings page reads/writes, migrated to the dsh 0.1.2-alpha.2 cohort.
+
+Host cohort notes:
+
+- The channel is registered with the two-argument
+  `ctx.connection.rpc.handle('/mineru-api', handler)`; callers read it through
+  `ctx.connection.rpc.call('/mineru-api', endpoint, payload)`. The handler
+  receives `(endpoint, payload, signal)` and returns a `ConnectionRpcResult`
+  (`{ ok: true, value }` | `{ ok: false, error }`) from
+  `@deepseek-ai/dsh-client-connection`; `error.code` stays the plugin's own
+  `internal`.
+- There is no per-channel `authority` option in this cohort. Connection mounts
+  every registered channel as a WebRoute that runs `requestRejection()` before
+  dispatch: the Host/Origin fence against the deployment's `trustedHosts`, then
+  browser-session authentication (401 without the session cookie). That is the
+  trusted-caller enforcement the old `{ authority: 'trusted-host' }` argument
+  asked for, so the argument is neither accepted nor required.
+- The settings page mounts through the official seat for a feature's own
+  settings page: `settings.section` (type home
+  `@deepseek-ai/dsh-client-ui-settings`, declared at runtime by
+  `@deepseek-ai/dsh-client-ui-settings-general`). The browser half injects
+  `['connection', 'locale', 'slots']` and keeps reading/writing through the
+  plugin's own `/mineru-api` channel. The keyed `settings.plugin.item` card in
+  the official Plugins section is a different seat driven by the official
+  settings remote, so this plugin does not adopt it.
+- The browser half ships as the client module system's lazy-CJS factory
+  artifact: `exports["./client"]` must call
+  `window.__ModuleLoader__.load({ id, factory })` with `id` equal to the package
+  name, because the host serves it to the page as a same-origin classic script.
+  A plain ESM `./client` export never registers, and the settings page stays out
+  of the boot graph.
 
 Release procedure (internal):
 
